<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What conveyors are used in automotive manufacturing?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Overhead power-and-free for body shop, skid conveyors for paint shop, slat/chain floor conveyors for final assembly, pallet transfer for component sub-assembly, and AGVs for flexible routing. Each shop uses conveyors optimized for its specific process.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">What is a power-and-free conveyor?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Uses two tracks: a power track with a continuous chain and a free track with independent trolleys. Trolleys engage/disengage the power chain to stop at stations while others continue. Enables mixed-model production with different dwell times.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">How are conveyors used for EV battery assembly?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Pallet transfer for cell module assembly, heavy-duty conveyors or AGVs for pack assembly, ESD-safe belt surfaces, thermal monitoring, and fire suppression integration. <a href="/conveyor-functions/indexing-conveyors/">Servo indexing</a> for robotic cell insertion.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">What is a skid conveyor?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Carries vehicle bodies on metal skid frames through paint shop processes. Chain-driven or friction-driven roller beds advance skids. The skid provides a universal interface for different body styles. Must withstand repeated paint oven cure cycles.</p>

</div>
